<title>RUSSIA: TABLE - Russian net reserves rise to 31.3 trln rbls.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Russian net reserves rise to 31.3 trln rbls.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's net international reserves rose to 31.3 trillion roubles on June 1 from 23.5 trillion roubles on May 1, the central bank said on Friday in its weekly bulletin.</p>
<p>The central bank issued the following data (trillions of roubles):</p>
<p>				   June 1	  May 1     June 1, 96</p>
<p> Monetary base		  148.2	    n/a	118.8</p>
<p>comprising</p>
<p>    Net currency reserves    31.3	   23.5	 35.7</p>
<p>    Net domestic assets     116.9	    n/a	 68.1.</p>
<p>NOTES - Some May data not available. Reserves in 1997 calculated at a rate of 5,560 roubles per dollar, in 1996 at 4,640 roubles per dollar. Rouble currently about 5,780 per dollar.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
